SUMMARY:Facebook
DESCRIPTION:published - Remember the first time you rode a bicycle? Or the 
 first time you spoke a language that wasn't your mother tongue? Or your fi
 rst hour on a computer at school?\n\nNew feels exciting and scary at once.
  Exciting because it's new. Scary because of everything we don't know yet.
  But not knowing something doesn't mean we can't learn it\, and the scary 
 part usually shrinks once we look at the details. So let's look.\n\nTake A
 I. The news is loud: it's amazing\, it's exciting\, it's frightening\, som
 etimes in the same headline.\n\nI'm learning AI in public\, so I started t
 his blog. It's called AI Business Lab.\n\nI work in finance and strategy\,
  so that's where I start\, not where I stop. I'll test AI on business prob
 lems wherever they show up\, from a budget table to building my own team o
 f agents.\n\nI like things structured and easy to follow\, and I'll break 
 down the complex terms and ideas the way I wish someone had done for me.\n
 \nRegularly\, I'll run one real task through AI and show you what happened
 \, mistakes included.\n\nIf you're starting too\, come along. Let's share\
 , help each other and learn together.\n\nCheers!\n\nP.S. This post was co-
 created by me and my Social Squad Agent team. I'll introduce them here\, s
 lowly.
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
